<title>SINGAPORE: World rice prices - November 21.</title>
<headline>World rice prices - November 21.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rice prices quoted by trading and official sources in the key producing nations of Thailand, Vietnam, India and the United States in U.S. dollars a tonne:</p>
<p>							     Nov 21    Nov 14</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct white B benchmark FOB Bangkok 320-350  330-360</p>
<p>India-25 pct broken(non-Basmati long grain)FOB 235	  240</p>
<p>India-15-10 pct broken FOB (west coast port)  265-285   275-285</p>
<p>Vietnam-5.0 percent broken FOB Saigon port    280-285   280-285</p>
<p>Vietnam-10 percent broken FOB Saigon port     270-275   275-280</p>
<p>U.S.-California medium grain ($ per cwt) 19.50-20.50 19.50-20.50 U.S.-Long grain Arkansas ($ per cwt)     19.50-20.50 19.50-20.50</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703305)</p>
